{"slug":"/students/subjects/physics/foundations/quantities/","source":"students/subjects/physics/foundations/quantities.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Fundamental & Derived Quantities | Physics Foundations","description":"","subject":"physics","body":"<div class=\"max-w-6xl mx-auto\">\n        <nav class=\"mb-8\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/foundations/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700\">← Back to Foundations</a>\n        </nav>\n\n        <div class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-8\">\n            <header class=\"mb-12\">\n                <h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Fundamental &amp; Derived Quantities</h1>\n                <p class=\"text-lg text-gray-600\">Understanding the basic and complex physical quantities that describe our universe</p>\n            </header>\n\n            <div class=\"grid gap-8\">\n                <!-- Introduction -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">What are Physical Quantities?</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">A physical quantity is any property that can be measured or calculated. Every physical quantity consists of two parts:</p>\n                        <ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700\">\n                            <li>A numerical value (magnitude)</li>\n                            <li>A unit of measurement</li>\n                        </ul>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Fundamental Quantities -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Fundamental (Base) Quantities</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">These are the basic quantities that cannot be expressed in terms of other quantities:</p>\n                        <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n                            <table class=\"w-full text-sm\">\n                                <thead>\n                                    <tr class=\"text-left\">\n                                        <th class=\"pb-4 pr-4 font-semibold\">Quantity</th>\n                                        <th class=\"pb-4 pr-4 font-semibold\">SI Unit</th>\n                                        <th class=\"pb-4 font-semibold\">Symbol</th>\n                                    </tr>\n                                </thead>\n                                <tbody class=\"text-gray-700\">\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">Length</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">meter</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3\">m</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">Mass</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">kilogram</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3\">kg</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">Time</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">second</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3\">s</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">Electric Current</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">ampere</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3\">A</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">Temperature</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">kelvin</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3\">K</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">Amount of Substance</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">mole</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3\">mol</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">Luminous Intensity</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">candela</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3\">cd</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                </tbody>\n                            </table>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Derived Quantities -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Derived Quantities</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">These quantities are expressed in terms of fundamental quantities:</p>\n                        <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n                            <table class=\"w-full text-sm\">\n                                <thead>\n                                    <tr class=\"text-left\">\n                                        <th class=\"pb-4 pr-4 font-semibold\">Quantity</th>\n                                        <th class=\"pb-4 pr-4 font-semibold\">Formula</th>\n                                        <th class=\"pb-4 pr-4 font-semibold\">SI Unit</th>\n                                        <th class=\"pb-4 font-semibold\">Unit Formula</th>\n                                    </tr>\n                                </thead>\n                                <tbody class=\"text-gray-700\">\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">Area</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">length × width</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">square meter</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3\">m²</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">Volume</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">length × width × height</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">cubic meter</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3\">m³</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">Velocity</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">displacement/time</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">meter per second</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3\">m/s</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">Acceleration</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">velocity/time</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">meter per second squared</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3\">m/s²</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">Force</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">mass × acceleration</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">newton</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3\">kg⋅m/s²</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                    <tr>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">Energy</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">force × displacement</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3 pr-4\">joule</td>\n                                        <td class=\"pb-3\">kg⋅m²/s²</td>\n                                    </tr>\n                                </tbody>\n                            </table>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Key Points -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Key Points to Remember</h2>\n                    <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">About Fundamental Quantities</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• They are independent of each other</li>\n                                <li>• They form the basis of all measurements</li>\n                                <li>• They have unique SI units</li>\n                                <li>• They can't be broken down further</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">About Derived Quantities</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• They are combinations of fundamental quantities</li>\n                                <li>• Their units can be expressed in terms of fundamental units</li>\n                                <li>• They often have special names (e.g., newton, joule)</li>\n                                <li>• They can be derived using dimensional analysis</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Practice Problems -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Practice Problems</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-4 text-gray-700\">\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-2\">Problem 1:</p>\n                                <p>Express pressure (force per unit area) in terms of fundamental quantities.</p>\n                                <p class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-blue-600\">Think: Force is kg⋅m/s², area is m². Final units will be kg/(m⋅s²)</p>\n                            </li>\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-2\">Problem 2:</p>\n                                <p>Identify whether density (mass per unit volume) is a fundamental or derived quantity. Express it in terms of fundamental units.</p>\n                                <p class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-blue-600\">Think: Consider the units of mass (kg) and volume (m³)</p>\n                            </li>\n                        </ol>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-indigo-100 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n        .content-card {\n            -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n            backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);\n            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n            box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n        }"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}